// The Sunken Library (bible 4.3, 8.3 [F 5.1]): an anchored library; Brother Ansel has read page 214 for thirty-eight
// years. The book is a history of the Halloways (5.4). Turn the page and he forgets the thirty-eight years.
// Library_2. Teodor will not turn it; he tells her so at the reading stair (Library_1).

title: Library_Teodor_Ansel
---
Teodor: He is reading. He has been reading for thirty-eight years. He is happy on that page.
Teodor: I will not turn it for you. May I say a thing you will not like? Neither should you. #plant:5.1
<<flag verdance.library.teodor_asked 1>>
===

title: Library_Ansel
---
<<if has_flag("verdance.library.page_turned")>>
    Ansel: Two hundred and fifteen. The owl had a daughter. I never knew that. Did you? #plant:5.4
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
<<if has_flag("verdance.library.decided")>>
    Ansel: Two hundred and fourteen. A marvellous page. I have only just begun it. #still
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Ansel: Two hundred and fourteen. A marvellous page. I have only just begun it.
Ansel: A history of the Halloways. The owl who kept the Atlas. It is very good about his family. #plant:5.4
Ansel: I am coming to the part about his daughter. Any moment now.
-> What's on the next page?
    Ansel: I do not know. That is the pleasure of it. I will know soon.
-> Can I turn it for you?
    Ansel: Would you? My wings are so tired. I have been holding it open a little while.
    <<jump Library_Ansel_Turn>>
-> ...
    Ansel: Yes. Quiet. It is a library.
<<flag verdance.library.decided 2>>
===

title: Library_Ansel_Turn
---
-> Turn the page.
    Ansel: Oh. Oh. Two hundred and fifteen.
    Ansel: Where is everyone? It was morning. Who are you? Who has let the dust in?
    <<flag verdance.library.page_turned 1>>
    <<flag verdance.library.decided 1>>
-> Leave it where it is.
    Ansel: Kind of you. Another time. There is no hurry. There never is, down here. #still
    <<flag verdance.library.decided 2>>
===
